{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"AC — botocore retry/timeout parity gap FILED as its own defect: 61d8-ff23-8ee0-4289 (elliptical-deep-whale), linked discovered_from this ticket (link_uuid fed50ce8-a9eb-491a-8c2e-594f1baa0830, verified by content).\n\nSubstance carried into it, so this cutover does not have to claim parity it does not have: src/rebar/llm/bedrock_model.py:88 is a bare BedrockProvider(region_name=region) with no botocore.config.Config(retries=...); the tenacity envelope and RetryConfig live ONLY in anthropic_model.py:114-150. Therefore llm_retry_max_attempts and timeout_s do NOT reach the Bedrock transport — Bedrock gets botocore stock client defaults, which do retry throttling and transient 5xx but are neither configured nor observable by rebar. The epic's 'first_class = full fidelity => equivalent retry and timeout per transport' is an unmet intention, not a landed property. This ticket writes the true posture into the runbook instead of fixing it, because the fix changes the provider builder and does not belong inside a production cutover."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785795612809938001,"uuid":"36c4cf31-383f-49ff-ba6e-2974f43a51c2"}